{
  "id": "augmentative-communication",
  "term": "augmentative communication",
  "definition": "Augmentative communication is an added way of communicating that uses a direct channel from the brain to an output device, without relying on muscle movement. In this source, it refers to brain-computer interface systems that translate detected brain signals into commands so people with neuromotor or nervous system injuries can operate devices and communicate.",
